{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Morning. Come on in and have a seat. What's brought you?",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): It's the nose, doctor. It's blocked completely, I can't breathe through it at all.",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (CAREGIVER): I'm Concepta, I stay with her on the weekdays. She's been miserable with it since the cold.",
  "[SEG0004] person_1 (DOCTOR): Thanks, Concepta. Is there discharge from the nose, or just the blockage?",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (PATIENT): Green stuff. Thick. I don't know, doctor, it's horrible.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long has that green discharge and the blockage been going?",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (PATIENT): Umm. I don't know, doctor. After the cold. A while, I think.",
  "[SEG0008] person_3 (CAREGIVER): The cold was a bit over two weeks ago. Blocked nose and the green mucus, that's been ten days.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right. Any pressure in the face?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Yes. A weight across the cheeks and up into the forehead.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): Does anything make that worse?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Bending down. Like, to the press for a cup. It throbs then. Err.",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (CAREGIVER): And she's tired. We're into the second week of her being wrecked. She left her tea go cold this morning, not like her.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): I am flat. No energy. I don't know.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Is there a headache on top of the pressure, or not?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Not a headache. I don't think so.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any fever? Shivers?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): I don't know, doctor. I don't think I've been hot.",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (CAREGIVER): I did the thermometer last night and it was normal. No shivering that I saw.",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (DOCTOR): Swelling round the eyes, or pain in them?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): No. The eyes are grand.",
  "[SEG0022] person_1 (DOCTOR): Cough, or short of breath?",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): A little cough in the mornings. Not short of breath, no.",
  "[SEG0024] person_1 (DOCTOR): What are you using for the nose?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): The spray, every day. Uh, the otravin from the chemist.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Two squirts each nostril, morning and night, the whole ten days. I did say that was a lot.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Mm. Otrivine. Any other medicines you take regular?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): The blood pressure tablet. I don't know the name, doctor.",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (CAREGIVER): Amlodipine, five milligrams, one every morning. Years, for the blood pressure. And paracetamol, two tablets, when the face is sore. Maybe twice a day this week.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (DOCTOR): Antihistamines, or another spray?",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (PATIENT): No. That's all. I think.",
  "[SEG0032] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any reactions to drugs? Anything you've been told not to take?",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Penicilin. I got welts, a red itchy rash over my chest and my arms. They told me never again.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (CAREGIVER): There's a card in the press at home. Hives. We don't let anyone give her penicillin.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): Let me say it back, so I've got it. Cold a bit over two weeks ago. Blocked nose and thick green discharge for ten days. Pressure in the cheeks and forehead, worse on bending.",
  "[SEG0036] person_1 (DOCTOR): Tiredness into a second week, and you said there was no headache. Otrivine morning and night, amlodipine five milligrams, and paracetamol for the face. Penicillin gives an itchy rash with welts, no fever, eyes grand. Not breathless, is that fair?",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (PATIENT): Well, actually. The head. I said it wasn't, but it is a headache. Sore over the eyes, and worse when I bend. I don't know why I said no.",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (CAREGIVER): She told me yesterday the head was sore, in fairness. I should've brought it up.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): That's useful, thank you. We'll count the headache. Let me look at you.",
  "[SEG0040] person_1 (DOCTOR): The lining of the nose is swollen on both sides, with green mucus there. Tender over the cheeks. Throat is a little red, and the lungs are clear. Temperature today is 36.8 celsius.",
  "[SEG0041] person_2 (PATIENT): Is 36.8 bad? I don't know, doctor.",
  "[SEG0042] person_1 (DOCTOR): No, that's a normal temperature. This sounds like sinusitis after the cold. Most of these settle without an antibiotic, even with the green discharge.",
  "[SEG0043] person_3 (CAREGIVER): So no antibiotic today?",
  "[SEG0044] person_1 (DOCTOR): Not to start today. And stop the otravin. Used this long, it keeps the nose blocked on you.",
  "[SEG0045] person_2 (PATIENT): Just stop it? I don't know. It's the only thing that opens me.",
  "[SEG0046] person_1 (DOCTOR): It rebounds, I'm afraid. Salt water rinses morning and night, paracetamol when the face aches, and carry on with the amlodipine as usual.",
  "[SEG0047] person_3 (CAREGIVER): And if she doesn't turn the corner?",
  "[SEG0048] person_1 (DOCTOR): That's the back-up. I'll write clarithromycin, by mouth, 500 mg twice a day for five days. Only start it if you're no better in five days. It isn't a penicillin, so it shouldn't bring that rash on.",
  "[SEG0049] person_1 (DOCTOR): If a fever spikes, or an eye swells, or the headache gets severe, don't wait. Come back here, or the emergency department if we're shut.",
  "[SEG0050] person_3 (CAREGIVER): I'll keep an eye. Do you need to see her again?",
  "[SEG0051] person_1 (DOCTOR): If it's not better in five days, come back and we'll review it, script or no script. Ring reception and they'll fit you in.",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (PATIENT): The bus was late, that's why we were all flustered coming in. Nothing else, I don't think.",
  "[SEG0053] person_1 (DOCTOR): Grand so. You've both got the plan. Mind yourselves."
 ],
